{#
  The source of truth for every plan export (Stage 02 PRD §12, §14).

  Rules for editing this file:
  - Never put a judgement in here. The template arranges what node 2.6.1
    already decided; a conditional that changes a status is a node change
    wearing a template's clothes.
  - Every long table states its own cap in the document. A table silently cut
    to 25 campaigns reads as a complete list, which is worse than no table.
  - `plan.md.j2` and `plan.html.j2` render the same sections in the same
    order. §14's acceptance compares them.
  - The draft watermark is not decoration. §14: a draft must not be able to
    circulate as a signed-off plan, in any format.
  - A line that ends in `{% endif %}` or `{% endfor %}` must be followed by
    `{{ "" }}`. `trim_blocks` eats the newline after a block tag, so without it
    the next line joins this one — and when the next line is `---`, markdown
    reads the pair as a setext heading and the separator silently becomes a
    title. An empty expression tag is not a block tag, so the newline survives.
#}
